<title>USA: CFTC grants dual trading exemption to Comex.</title>
<headline>CFTC grants dual trading exemption to Comex.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commodity Futures Trading Commission said Wednesday it granted a dual trading exemption for gold and silver contracts to the Comex division of New York Mercantile Exchange.</p>
<p>CFTC said Comex maintained a trade monitoring system able to detect any dual trading or other trading violations.</p>
<p>The agency's dual trading porhibition forbids a floor broker from executing trades for both himself and for customers in the same contract during a trading session.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk, 202 898 8467))</p>
